NEURAL NETWORK ZOO  (Asimov / van Veen 2016 style)
Legend of cell types
  I  Input          nI Noisy input       bI Backfed input
  H  Hidden         pH Probabilistic H   sH Spiking H
  O  Output         mO Match I/O
  R  Recurrent      M  Memory            dM Diff memory
  K  Kernel         C  Conv / pool

FUNDAMENTALS
  Activation a = f(Wx + b)     Loss L = measure(y, yhat)
  Backprop   dW = dL/dW        SGD/Adam update W := W - lr * dW
  Recurrence h_t = f(h_{t-1}, x_t)
  Conv       y = K * x         Residual y = F(x) + x
  Latent     z ~ q(z|x)        Adversarial min_G max_D V(D,G)

PERCEPTRON (P)
  I -- O
  y = step(w·x + b)

FEED FORWARD (FF)
  I -- H -- O
  y = f2(W2 f1(W1 x + b1) + b2)

RADIAL BASIS (RBF)
  I -- H(phi) -- O
  phi_i = exp(-||x-c_i||^2 / 2s^2)

DEEP FEED FORWARD (DFF)
  I -- H -- H -- H -- O
  stacked FF, more capacity, vanishing-grad risk

RNN
  I -- R -- O
       ^
       |
  h_t = tanh(W_h h_{t-1} + W_x x_t)

LSTM
  I -- M -- O     gates: i f o
  c_t = f*c_{t-1} + i*tanh(...)
  h_t = o * tanh(c_t)

GRU
  I -- dM -- O    gates: z r
  h_t = (1-z)*h_{t-1} + z*h_tilde

AUTOENCODER (AE)
  I -- H -- O(=I)
  reconstruct x from bottleneck z

VAE
  I -- pH -- O     z ~ N(mu, sigma)
  L = recon + KL(q(z|x) || p(z))

DENOISING AE (DAE)
  nI -- H -- O
  train on corrupted x, recover clean x

SPARSE AE (SAE)
  I -- H -- O
  + sparsity penalty on hidden activations

MARKOV CHAIN (MC)
  pH -- pH -- pH   P(s_{t+1}|s_t)

HOPFIELD (HN)
  fully connected attractor net
  energy E = -1/2 s^T W s    recall by energy descent

BOLTZMANN (BM)
  pH fully connected, stochastic
  P ~ exp(-E/T)

RESTRICTED BM (RBM)
  I -- pH     bipartite, no intra-layer edges
  contrastive divergence training

DEEP BELIEF NET (DBN)
  stacked RBMs then fine-tune
  I -- pH -- pH -- O

DEEP CONV NET (DCN / CNN)
  I -- C -- C -- H -- O
  conv + pool + fully connected
  y = f(K * x + b)

DECONV NET (DN)
  I -- C^T -- C^T -- O
  upsample / transposed conv

DCIGN
  encoder CNN -> latent graphics vars -> decoder
  inverse graphics flavor of AE

GAN
  G: z -- H -- fake
  D: real/fake -- H -- O
  min_G max_D  E[log D(x)] + E[log(1-D(G(z)))]

LIQUID STATE MACHINE (LSM)
  sH reservoir, readout trained only
  liquid dynamics, sparse random recurrency

EXTREME LEARNING MACHINE (ELM)
  I -- H(fixed rand) -- O
  only output weights solved (least squares)

ECHO STATE NET (ESN)
  I -- R(fixed reservoir) -- O
  only readout trained, echo-state property

DEEP RESIDUAL (DRN / ResNet)
  I -- H --+-- H --+-- O
           |       |
           +-------+
  y = F(x) + x     eases deep training

KOHONEN / SOM (KN)
  I -- H(grid)
  winner-take-all + neighborhood update
  topographic map of input manifold

SVM (not strictly NN, often in zoo)
  I -- K -- O
  max-margin  y = sign(sum a_i y_i K(x,x_i) + b)

NEURAL TURING MACHINE (NTM)
  I -- H -- O
         |
        M controller + external memory
  read/write heads, addressing
